Z||000005||Haze_Performance||11-05-2000||07:34 AM||||Junk yard ripoff (part 2)<P>I went to 6 yards this weekend.. I found one with a GREAT shape 88 Coupe. It had all the dot type dash panels (MINT!!) I asked how much for the panels & they said "No panels, You buy whole dash"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> The sons of b*t*hes!!<P><BR>Sometimes I think the people that work as junk yards never read the sign that says "Salvage Yard" on the front of the building.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/goodlogo1_1.gif"> ||||reg||13
Z||000006||theogre||11-05-2000||11:59 AM||||for $130 I got both complete P/W doors, the dash in good shape, the window wiring harness, a leather steering wheel in soso shape, and assorted other stuff.<P>The dash and P/W doors are now in the car. (Power Windows are a nessesity not an option on Fiero.) The steering wheel has been cleaned and I also have since gotten a leather shift knob to match. I haven't decided to put them on yet. ||||reg||7
Z||000007||rogergarrison||11-05-2000||12:28 PM||||way too much. yard around here will only pay a max of $75-100 for a car that you drive in to salvage. shop around and you could find a whole car for that, get tons of ther spare parts too.||||reg||1
